* A congruence reaching the body of a finite sum and of a finite product: tools/congr.py cites the ` s ` variants ` sumeq2sdv ` and ` prodeq2sdv ` , whose hypothesis is under the plain antecedent.

s1::id |- ( f = C -> f = C )
c1:s1:oveq1d |- ( f = C -> ( f x. k ) = ( C x. k ) )
c2:c1:sumeq2sdv |- ( f = C -> sum_ k e. ( 1 ... N ) ( f x. k ) = sum_ k e. ( 1 ... N ) ( C x. k ) )
